      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-04-16T14:01:44Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Sorry it is not about the pointer itself which is __initdata but the entire initial fdt region being discarded. Note that arm doesn\u0027t use\n`unflatten_and_copy_device_tree` but `unflatten_device_tree` and copying is omitted: arm seems to operate all the time on the same fdt while x86 switches to its copy.\n\nFor x86, see `x86_flattree_get_config`:\n- initial dtb is `early_memremap(initial_dtb, map_len)`\n- set to `initial_boot_params` via `early_init_dt_verify`\n- fdt is copied by `unflatten_and_copy_device_tree` and `initial_boot_params` is updated to point to new copy\n- initial dtb is discarded later on via `early_memunmap(dt, map_len);`",
      "parentUuid": "6ccd08f6_6d3735f0",
      "revId": "7eb1c90f776cec249f0a938310de751e3cbdbc8f",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
